## 5. Allowed — Language & OOP

| Allowed | Notes |
|---------|-------|
| `virtual` | Required for polymorphism |
| `virtual ~Base()` | Required when deleting derived via `Base*` |
| `virtual func() = 0` | Pure virtual / abstract base class |
| `nullptr` | Preferred null pointer |
| `new` / `delete` / `new[]` / `delete[]` | Manual memory management |
| `std::string` | Allowed |
| STL containers & algorithms | `vector`, `list`, `map`, `unordered_map`, `stack`, `queue`, `priority_queue`, `<algorithm>` — allowed in the final project; choose by access pattern |
| `try` / `throw` / `catch` | For real errors (constructor failure, invalid `operator[]`, etc.) |
| `dynamic_cast`, `typeid` | When safe downcast / RTTI is needed |
| `const`, references, `friend` | Core course topics |
| `template <class T>` / `template <typename T>` | Templates; class template bodies in `.h` |
| Include guards `#ifndef NAME_H` | Required on every header |
| `public` inheritance | `class Derived : public Base` |
| `protected` members / protected base constructor | When derived needs access / only derived may construct base |
| Operator overloading when meaning is clear | `=`, `==`, `<`, `[]`, `++`, `+=`, `<<`, `>>`, etc. |
| `using namespace std;` | Match existing project files |

