## 9. Required — Class & File Design

| Rule | Detail |
|------|--------|
| Include guard every `.h` | `#ifndef FILE_H` / `#define FILE_H` / `#endif` — **not** `#pragma once` |
| Split `.h` / `.cpp` | Declarations in header, definitions in cpp (except class templates → all in `.h`) |
| Member fields | `m_` prefix (`m_score`, `m_name`) |
| Static counters | `s_` prefix (`s_next_serial`) |
| Getters / non-mutating methods | Mark `const` |
| Read-only parameters | `const T&` |
| Polymorphism | `virtual` on base methods; derived implements **without** `override` |
| Polymorphic delete | `virtual ~Base()` on base |
| Abstract base | Pure virtual `= 0`; never instantiate the ABC |
| Init list | Use for const/ref members, base constructor args, members without default constructor |
| Copy constructor form | `ClassName(const ClassName& other)` |
| One class per file pair (typical) | e.g. `Player.h` + `Player.cpp` |

```cpp
// Polymorphism — course style (no override)
class Base {
public:
    virtual ~Base() {}
    virtual void doAction() = 0;
};

class Derived : public Base {
public:
    void doAction() { /* ... */ }
};

Base* p = new Derived();
p->doAction();
delete p;  // needs virtual ~Base()
```

